  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or rendered the scene in a browser, so the orbit and framing are untested.\n\nThe scene is built from three instanced nodes plus a ground plane:\n- **Instances:** 8,000 trees use cylinder trunks and cone canopies, and 2,000 rocks use squashed spheres. Each kind is one `instances.*` node, so it is one draw call.\n- **Placement:** positions come from a seeded LCG (seed 20240607), so the forest is the same on every load. Everything sits inside a 70 m radius on a 260 m ground plane.\n- **Colour:** canopies get per-instance HSL greens and rocks get per-instance grey-brown tones.\n- **Light and fog:** there is one shadow-casting directional light, plus a hemisphere fill that I added. Fog is `effects.fog` (exponential) with density 0.0035. The fog colour matches the background.\n- **Camera:** it uses `camera.orbit` and `interactions.orbit` with `autoRotate: 0.15` rad/s, so it circles at about 40 s per lap. The eye is at (0, 85, 120) looking at (0, 2, 0), with near 20 and far 450 so the whole forest should stay in view. I took that framing from the docs' forest recipe, which uses a similar position.\n- **Ready flag:** after `await app.ready()` and two animation frames, the code sets `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true`. The engine runs its own `requestAnimationFrame` loop.\n\n",
